From 7fb3686ca347109c92bbc6026433bf839cca9068 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AKENO NETWORK <noreply@akeno.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:50:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AKENO direct entry 4.1: link mode by default, a safe Settings
 root, diagnostics

The first direct entry failed on a PS5 (FW 12.20): the plugin's page was
served as the Settings root, ShellUI's plugin bridge dropped about 13 s later,
the daemon re-injected a new SceShellUI and controller input stayed dead.

- [shortcuts] toolbox_target_mode=link|root, default link: the shortcut
  opens the Toolbox route unchanged, and the Toolbox root lists the
  toolbox_target plugin's page first and selected (the link the Plugins page
  has). The Settings root is never replaced in link mode. Root mode is the
  OnionHEN?Plugin=<ID> takeover, now opt-in.
- Root mode serves the plugin's root page with root setting_list
  id_debug_settings, like every other Settings root (the Toolbox root and the
  Cheats page of OnionHEN?Cheats); the takeover used the page's own control
  id. The page owns no parent (ToolboxUiState::enter_settings_root).
- direct_entry.hpp: a pending request is taken once, expires after 15 s and
  is cancelled by any other OnionHEN route; repeated shortcuts within 2 s are
  one request; a plugin without a page opens the Toolbox. A Settings root
  served by any other route drops plugin pages a closed Settings left open.
- A session file in /system_tmp names the SceShellUI holding a session; a
  SceShellUI that starts while one is open after recent activity turns root
  mode off until restart (the shortcut opens the Toolbox) and says so.
- AKENO_DIRECT: log lines for every step (shortcut, URI, redirect, root
  served, root activated, page shown/popped, press outcome, session end) and
  a 60 s input watch after it (whether ShellUI reads the pad, button changes,
  one line per 5 s). No control ids or values are logged.
- x64 relocator: compare the jmp [rip+0] prefix byte by byte; the 6-byte
  memcmp read past the last instruction (ASan, test_x64_relocator).
- Host tests: direct_entry suite (12) and plugin_ui_direct_entry_flow
  driving the hook steps against the real registry, renderer, page stack and
  ToolboxUiState; the root-page test now checks the root setting_list id.
